### Lab 10: Set operations (Riak Data Types API; support/configuration dependent)
### This is an illustrative Riak set CRDT request. Confirm the endpoint/content-type
### required by your installed Riak release and enable the appropriate bucket type.
### Many releases use the Data Types API for sets, rather than storing a plain JSON list.
curl -i -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8098/types/sets/buckets/user_interests/datatypes/U101 \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"add":["analytics","design","databases"]}'

### Read current set
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8098/types/sets/buckets/user_interests/datatypes/U101

### Set endpoint and request syntax vary across Riak versions. To remove an element,
### submit a remove operation using the Data Types API format supported by your release.
